WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.757
Phone validation first strips punctuation and other non-digit characters.

00:00:04.757 --> 00:00:08.607
Then it checks whether the resulting candidate has ten digits.

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:12.472
Missing values are separated from invalid-shaped values.

00:00:12.472 --> 00:00:18.802
This is a good pattern: normalize representation first, then apply the validation rule.

00:00:18.802 --> 00:00:24.017
Standardization should make equivalent values comparable without inventing facts.

00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:30.322
Lowercasing an email or normalizing a known category map is different from guessing what an ambiguous value

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:36.333
was supposed to mean. Good cleaning reduces representation noise while preserving uncertainty.
